p.src:
The phrase energy density can tempt us to look only at $T_{00}$, but Einstein’s equation couples to the whole tensor. In a local orthonormal rest frame, an isotropic medium has $T_{\hat\mu\hat\nu}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \rho & 0 & 0 & 0\\
    0 & p & 0 & 0\\
    0 & 0 & p & 0\\
    0 & 0 & 0 & p
  \end{pmatrix}.$ With one index raised, the same convention reads $T^{\hat\mu}{}_{\hat\nu}
  =
  \operatorname{diag}(\rho,-p,-p,-p).$ Writing both forms prevents a common sign confusion.

