p.src:
Algebraically, $\Lambda$ may be left with the geometry, $G_{\mu\nu}+\Lambda g_{\mu\nu}=8\pi G T_{\mu\nu},$ or moved to the matter side, $G_{\mu\nu}
  =
  8\pi G
  \left(
  T_{\mu\nu}+T^{(\Lambda)}_{\mu\nu}
  \right),
  \qquad
  T^{(\Lambda)}_{\mu\nu}
  =
  -\frac{\Lambda}{8\pi G}g_{\mu\nu},$ where $c=1$. The second notation interprets the cosmological constant as vacuum stress-energy. It has energy density and pressure related by $p_\Lambda=-\rho_\Lambda.$ Whether it is written as geometry or vacuum energy, the measurable equation is the same.

