p.src:
Light can orbit a Schwarzschild black hole, but the circular null orbit is unstable. If $r_s=\frac{2GM}{c^2}$ denotes the horizon radius, the photon sphere lies at $\boxed{
  r_{\rm ph}
  =
  \frac{3GM}{c^2}
  =
  \frac32 r_s.}$ This is the corrected value previewed in the discussion: three halves of the horizon radius, not three horizon radii.

