p.src:
Now consider vacuum with a cosmological constant. From $R_{\mu\nu}
  -\frac12 g_{\mu\nu}R
  +\Lambda g_{\mu\nu}
  =0,$ contract with $g^{\mu\nu}$ in four spacetime dimensions: $\begin{aligned}
  R-\frac12(4)R+4\Lambda&=0,
  \notag\\
  R&=4\Lambda,
  \\
  R_{\mu\nu}&=\Lambda g_{\mu\nu}.
  \end{aligned}$ The sign follows the placement of $+\Lambda g_{\mu\nu}$ in Eq. ; moving that term or choosing the opposite curvature convention changes intermediate signs. The invariant lesson is that nonzero $\Lambda$ supports a vacuum of constant Ricci curvature.

